UID:4e001d23c7221efb@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260928T231502Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Attention Trading Partners: Refresher Trainin
 g for New MaineCare Partner Portal
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Attention Trading Partners: Refresher Training for New 
 MaineCare Partner Portal\nAttention Trading Partners: Refresher Training f
 or New MaineCare Partner Portal\nSep 28\, 2026\nAs a reminder\, the new Ma
 ineCare Partner Portal is scheduled to go live on\nOctober 12\, 2026\, at 
 8:00 AM\n. The new portal will replace the current HealthPAS Online Portal
  and provide enhanced functionality to support Trading Partner operations.
  We are adding additional live\, virtual instructor-led training sessions 
 to help Trading Partners prepare for the transition.\nAs a reminder\, reco
 rded training sessions\, training materials\, user guides\, Q&A documents 
 from training sessions\, and supporting resources are available through th
 e\nMMIS Learning Center\nand will continue to be available after go-live.\
 nPlease share this training information with staff responsible for claims\
 , authorizations\, referrals\, account maintenance\, and portal administra
 tion activities. Staff should not wait for refresher training to become fa
 miliar with the materials.\nKey Reminders\nTrading Partner Administrator (
 R7) accounts will be migrated to the new portal.\nAdditional users will be
  invited and managed by Trading Partner Administrators after go-live.\nTra
 ding Partner Administrators (R7 users) should prepare for portal access an
 d account setup activities by reviewing the training materials available i
 n the MMIS Learning Center before go-live.\nMaineCare Partner Portal Refre
 sher Training Sessions\nParticipants may register for any session that ali
 gns with their role and responsibilities. Please see\nthis e-message\nfor 
 a description of each course.\nTraining\nDates & Times (ET)\nME - TPT Refr
 esher - Migrated Trading Partner Log In and Account Maintenance Training (
 ILC)\n- this course is only for Admin (R7) users\nMonday\, October 5\, 9:0
 0 – 10:30\nWednesday\, October 7\, 11:00 AM – 12:30 PM\nME - TPT Refre
 sher - \nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/atten
 tion-trading-partners-refresher-training-new-mainecare-partner-portal-2026
 -09-28
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/attention-
 trading-partners-refresher-training-new-mainecare-partner-portal-2026-09-2
 8
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:99b2ba54757f82cf@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260928T231444Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] October 2026
DESCRIPTION:O&M Newsletter\, October 2026\nMaine Department of Environment
 al Protection sent this bulletin at 09/28/2026 11:57 AM EDT\nOCTOBER 2026\
 nIn this issue:\nDon't Miss Out: Participate in the FREE EPA Cybersecurity
  Series Today.\nCelebrating the Retirement of Two Dedicated DEP Employees 
 This October.\nDMR-QA Study 46 Open!\nTraining Highlights.\nIndustry Profi
 le: James Galasyn Serving 40 years in the Environmental Laboratory Field.\
 nCelebrating Innovative Water Professionals.\nFor Practice.\nDon't Miss Ou
 t: Participate in the FREE EPA Cybersecurity Series Today.\nCheck out the 
 October schedule for this comprehensive line-up of no-cost EPA Cybersecuri
 ty Webinars.\nCybersecurity 102\n- October 6\, 2026. Take a deeper look at
  Operational Technology (OT) cybersecurity and learn practical steps for n
 avigating today’s threats.\nCybersecurity 103\n- October 8\, 2026. Under
 stand current threats\, risks\, and vulnerabilities facing water systems a
 nd how to stay informed.\nCybersecurity 104\n- October 13\, 2026. Get simp
 le\, low‑cost best practices tailored for small and resource‑constrain
 ed utilities.\nCybersecurity Refresher\n- October 15\, 2026. Reinforce fou
 ndational concepts from Cyber 101\, 102\, and 103.\nCybersecurity 201\n- O
 ctober 20\, 2026. Explore how AI supports defenders and attackers—and le
 arn how to use it safely.\nCybersecurity 202\n- October 22\, 2026. Learn p
 ractical Zero Trust steps to strengthen access controls and protect Inform
 ation Technology (IT)/Operational Technology (OT) environments.\nWater Cyb
 ersecurity Assessment Tool (WCAT) Webinar\n- October 27\, 2026. See how EP
 A's WCAT can assess cybersecurity gaps at water and wastewater systems.\nC
 ybersecurity Procurement Checklist Tool Training\n- October 28\, 2026. Lea
 rn how to evaluate vendors using EPA’s procurement checklist.\nCybersecu
 rity 203\n- October 29\, 2026. Identify and reduce risks from vendors\, co
 ntractors\, and other third parties.\nCelebrating the Retirement of Two De
 dicated DEP Employees This October.\nGary Brooks - Eastern Maine Complian\
 nhttps://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/MEDEP/bulletins/42c5d6a
URL:https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/MEDEP/bulletins/42c5d6a
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:91af66b268594b54@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260928T134837Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Attention Trading Partners: MIHMS Upgrade Oct
 ober Payment Cycle Changes and System Access Limitations
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Attention Trading Partners: MIHMS Upgrade October Payme
 nt Cycle Changes and System Access Limitations\nAttention Trading Partners
 : MIHMS Upgrade October Payment Cycle Changes and System Access Limitation
 s\nSep 28\, 2026\nAs\npreviously communicated\n\, the Office of MaineCare 
 Services (OMS) is preparing to launch an upgraded version of MIHMS\, Maine
 Care’s claims processing system. The upgrade is currently scheduled to g
 o live on October 10\, 2026. To support a smooth transition\, OMS must imp
 lement temporary system access limitations and adjustments to payment cycl
 es in October.\nFrom Friday\, October 2 at 8:00 PM until Monday\, October 
 12 at 8:00 AM\, MIHMS will be in a “data freeze” while OMS completes f
 inal system readiness and transition activities.\nPlease note that we have
  updated the\nFAQ\npreviously shared\, as of September 21\, 2026.\nChanges
  to October payment cycles:\nReview this information and plan billing acco
 rdingly to prepare for the transition.\nPayment Cycle Date\nType of Cycle\
 nClaim Submission Deadline for Inclusion in Payment Cycle*\nWednesday\, 9/
 30/26\nLast regular payment cycle before the data freeze\nFriday\, 9/25/26
 \, 5:00 AM\nThursday\, 10/1/26\nExtra payment cycle before the data freeze
 \nWednesday\, 9/30/26\, 5:00 AM\nThere will be no payment on Wednesday\, O
 ctober 7.\nThursday\, 10/15/26\nFirst payment cycle after data freeze\, in
  upgraded system\nSecure File Transfer Protocol (SFTP) submission: Continu
 ous through data freeze up to Tuesday\, 10/13/26\, 2:00 PM\nPortal submiss
 ion:\nBefore data freeze: Friday\, 10/2/26\, 7:59 PM\nAfter data freeze: T
 uesday\, 10/13/26\, 2:00 PM\nWednesday\, 10/21/26\nRegular payment cycle\,
  in upgraded system\nFriday\, 10/16/26\, 5:00 AM\n*As always\, timely subm
 ission does not guarantee that the claim will process in time for the next
  payment cycle. OMS may take up to 30 days to process and pay a claim\, de
 pending on any edits or issue\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/pr
 ovider-bulletins/attention-trading-partners-mihms-upgrade-october-payment-
 cycle-changes-and-system-access-4
