DTSTAMP:20260925T213238Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Maine Blue Economy Week - September 28 throug
 h October 2
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, Maine's relationship with the ocean has always bee
 n dynamic\, shaped by changing communities\, resources\, markets\, and con
 ditions\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, from the earliest Indigenous traditions of fish
 ing\, harvesting\, and boatbuilding\, to the shipyards that continue to co
 nnect Maine to the world\, our people have long adapted to changing circum
 stances and found new ways to work on and with the sea\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, 
 many of the practices we recognize today as Maine traditions were once inn
 ovations themselves\, developed by generations of Maine people who embrace
 d new techniques\, technologies\, and ideas to pursue new opportunities wh
 ile respecting the natural limits of the Gulf of Maine\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, 
 Maine's fishermen\, sea farmers\, boatbuilders\, engineers\, entrepreneurs
 \, scientists\, researchers\, and inventors continue this tradition of ing
 enuity\, mastering traditional craftsmanship\, innovating new marine techn
 ologies and practices\, and advancing ocean science\, climate adaptation\,
  and blue biotechnology\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, as the Gulf of Maine experience
 s rapid change\, the tenacity\, expertise\, and spirit of innovation that 
 have long defined Maine's working waterfronts are more important than ever
  as we adapt to new conditions and pursue new opportunities\; and\nWHEREAS
 \n\, the future of Maine's blue economy depends on continued investment in
  the people\, research\, businesses\, and working waterfronts that have al
 ways transformed necessity into innovation\, and innovation into the Maine
  we know today\;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mil
 ls\, Governor of the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim the week of Septe
 mber 28-October 2\, 2026 as\nMaine Blue Economy Week\nand I encourage all 
 Maine people to recognize and celebrate the ingenuity\, expertise\, and en
 trepreneurial spirit that has sustained our connection to the ocean and wi
 ll help shape the future of Maine's blue economy.\nIn testimony whereof\, 
 I have caused\nthe Great Seal of the State to be\nhereunto affixed GIVEN u
 nder my\nh\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclam
 ations/2026-09-maine-blue-economy-week-september-28-through-october-2
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-09-maine-blue-economy-week-september-28-through-october-2
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
