UID:b70d9d69cee4c68a@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260925T170739Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Secretary of State warns of misleading electi
 on information websites\, online information
DESCRIPTION:Voters urged to look for .gov websites for official\, trusted 
 voter information\nAUGUSTA\, MAINE\n– Secretary of State Shenna Bellows 
 today warned Mainers to be vigilant when viewing voting information online
 . This included raising awareness of private sites that may give the false
  impression – by name\, URL\, and/or design – that it is an official e
 lection website.\n“It is becoming increasingly difficult to distinguish 
 what is real and what isn’t online\,” said\nSecretary Bellows\n. “AI
  and other automated tools help partisan operatives or cybercriminals crea
 te websites that look official even when they’re not. While some non-gov
 ernmental sites about voting present accurate information\, many do not.
 ”\nMany sites are designed to encourage citizens to register to vote and
  may in fact redirect visitors to official sites. However\, many sites may
  require visitors to enter their personal information before they are redi
 rected. Official state addresses will include .gov. For example\, Mainers 
 can register to vote at\nhttps://www.maine.gov/vote\nor find official elec
 tion information by visiting the Secretary of State’s website at\nhttps:
 //www.maine.gov/sos\n.\n“If you don’t see .gov in the web address\, it
  is not an official state government website\,”\nSecretary Bellows\nsaid
 . “If you are being asked to enter personal information like name and em
 ail address before you get to an official .gov link\, then someone else is
  getting your private data. Instead of giving out private information to s
 ites that might try to scam you or steal your data\, go straight to the so
 urce at maine.gov/vote.”\nSecretary Bellows also encouraged voters to be
  careful when viewing election information on social media and always rese
 arch and vet the information that they read.\n“There is unfortunately so
  much misinformation and disinformation out there\, it can be overwhelming
  and difficult to know what’s true and what’s not\,” said\nSecretary
  Bellows\n. “Everyone can play a part in reducing anxiety about the upco
 ming election\nhttps://www.maine.gov/sos/news/secretary-state-warns-mislea
 ding-election-information-websites-online-information
URL:https://www.maine.gov/sos/news/secretary-state-warns-misleading-electi
 on-information-websites-online-information
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
